//? Title: Spearman, Kendall and quadrant association
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A simulated sensor response follows a monotonic nonlinear calibration curve
with random error. Rounding the second readout creates ties. Compare three
measures of association on the same paired data. Median lines in the plot show
which observations enter each quadrant.
)

> Simulate, test and plot

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/rank_association.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

namespace sp = dm::stats;
using dm::graphics::RPlot;

int main() {
    dm::set_seed(42);
    const auto x = dm::runif(-2, 2, 32);
    const auto noise = dm::rnorm(0, 0.7, 32);
    dm::Vector<> y(x.size());
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < x.size(); ++i)
        y[i] = std::round(2 * (x[i] + 0.22 * std::pow(x[i], 3) + noise[i])) / 2;

    const auto spearman = sp::spearman_correlation_test(x, y);
    const auto kendall = sp::kendall_correlation_test(x, y);
    const auto quadrant = sp::quadrant_test(x, y);
    std::print("| Method | Association | p-value |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto* test : {&spearman, &kendall, &quadrant})
        std::print("| {} | {:.3f} | {:.4g} |\n", test->method, test->estimate1, test->p_value);
    std::print("\nQuadrant test retained {:.0f} of {} pairs.\n", quadrant.parameter1, x.size());

    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    RPlot::create().points(x, y, "simulated pair", {36, 105, 172})
        .abline_v(dm::median(x)).abline_h(dm::median(y))
        .title("Monotonic calibration with rounded readouts")
        .x_label("Reference measurement").y_label("Rounded readout")
        .save_svg("build/rank_association.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| Method | Association | p-value |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| Spearman's rank correlation rho | 0.945 | 4.576e-16 |
| Kendall rank correlation (tie-corrected normal approximation) | 0.837 | 6.039e-11 |
| Median quadrant association (conditional Fisher exact) | 0.931 | 2.063e-07 |

Quadrant test retained 29 of 32 pairs.
\image(figures/rank_association.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Paired observations with median lines that define the four quadrants.)
\alttext(Paired observations with median lines that define the four quadrants.)

> Interpretation

Spearman uses average ranks and a t approximation. Kendall tau-b counts
concordant and discordant pairs while adjusting for ties. These rounded data
use Kendall's tie-corrected normal calibration. An untied sample of at most
50 pairs instead gets an exact reference. The quadrant test discards points
on either median line and applies a conditional Fisher exact test to the signs
of the retained pairs.

> References

- [R correlation tests|https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/cor.test.html]
- [Blomqvist, On a Measure of Dependence Between Two Random Variables|https://doi.org/10.1214/aoms/1177729754]
